{"kind":"002-S1-blocked-repair-remediation-review","review_target_revision":"2ed92fff8db5278f975b71019f919f645c0edd7872189e652a05ea4c483f37ee","execution_id":"execute-step-result-f3ba78f3d501e625493954b32c6c3391f172ad3b539129e0","scope":"Only continuation/append, conflicting overlap and their test effectiveness. No Runtime diagnosis, business writes, budget extension or clean acceptance.","resolved_fingerprints":[],"unresolved_fingerprints":["finding-63fad9ec0fd6323304a2f9481d895779","finding-f055a9eb19e6da4e496a31f4bea6b66a","finding-910c21597a109a7f4018404e778c8ca6"],"findings":[{"fingerprint":"finding-63fad9ec0fd6323304a2f9481d895779","priority":"P1","status":"unresolved","confidence":"high","evidence_kind":"static code trace plus existing regression execution","location":"native/codex-rollout-collector/src/protocol/target_source.rs:1413-1417","improvement":"The current small-fixture prefix continuation and known suffix reach ForwardAppend instead of oscillating or returning no cursor.","remaining":"The terminal promotion read returns vec![backend.plan_full(spec)] before the max_segment_bytes windowing at line1420. read_plan.rs:364-365,502-516 plan_full/plan_forward_mode only validate common limits, not segment length. target_source.rs:1530-1545 collects every record in the single plan into Vec before any spool handoff. Thus for an otherwise valid file larger than max_segment_bytes, known suffix or a complete-coverage Backfill continuation rereads the full snapshot as one oversized segment and retains full raw history. This violates the existing C1 bounded-continuation requirement, so the existing finding cannot be fully resolved. No fresh adversarial execution was performed.","required":"Preserve bounded physical windows and raw-record residency on the promotion-read continuation branch; do not merely trade the old loop for a whole-file resident read."},{"fingerprint":"finding-910c21597a109a7f4018404e778c8ca6","priority":"P1","status":"unresolved","confidence":"high","evidence_kind":"static counterexample; not claimed as an executed reproduction","location":"native/codex-rollout-collector/src/protocol/target_mapping.rs:600-615","improvement":"Single retained-record self-match is excluded; once overlap_conflict is detected, append formal cursor publication is suppressed.","remaining":"retained.iter().find searches all resident records, not only previously accepted records. Counterexample: accepted original A at source position P is in the earlier spool; resident last window additionally contains two identical altered copies B1/B2 of P (different timestamp/raw/ordinal/parse_error from A). for_each_record replays A first, which is New and advances frontier. B1 later matches B2 and B2 matches B1 because pointer inequality only excludes self. Both become Duplicate, neither sets overlap_conflict, original clean summary remains eligible for Canonical/ForwardAppend. The comparison has proved B1=B2, not B=A. This is the same conflicting-overlap invariant, not a new product feature.","required":"Only previously accepted identity/content evidence may prove duplicate; if original comparison evidence was discarded, preserve conflict/fail-closed rather than letting unaccepted copies prove each other."},{"fingerprint":"finding-f055a9eb19e6da4e496a31f4bea6b66a","priority":"P2","status":"unresolved","confidence":"high","evidence_kind":"test source inspection and 6/6 execution","location":"native/codex-rollout-collector/tests/rollout_blockers.rs:711-890;469-535","improvement":"Terminal cursor assertions now mandatory; cross-window tool inputs/outputs/turn IDs/key equality, exact overlap, append turn content and single-copy conflicts are materially stronger.","remaining":"three_entrypoints uses default limits and checks only range/cursor terminal shape, not bounded segments/resident records or complete history equality followed by unchanged cursor/checkpoint append on that continuation path. Separate multi-window test has no known range/cursor and never enters plan_full promotion-read branch. Conflict controls mutate a resident record with original still resident and never cover spooled original plus two mutually matching altered copies. All six tests therefore pass while the two inspected defects remain. No extra test suite is required; strengthen the existing admitted cases.","required":"Use the existing tests with total source > per-segment limit for prefix and suffix continuation, verify every physical window/resident handoff and terminal history/append behavior; include conflicting overlap whose accepted original is no longer resident."}],"validation":{"commands":[{"command":"cargo test --locked --manifest-path native/codex-rollout-collector/Cargo.toml --test rollout_blockers","exit_code":0,"passed":6,"failed":0},{"command":"cargo test --locked --manifest-path native/codex-rollout-collector/Cargo.toml --test conformance --test stage2_input","exit_code":0,"passed":34,"failed":0},{"command":"git diff --check","exit_code":1,"output":"docs/workflow/task-basis/TASK_BASIS-002.md:210: trailing whitespace. +      /prepare-task "}],"environment":"CARGO_TARGET_DIR=OS TEMP/termlink-rollout-blockers-target; no broad stage4/Node suite run","note":"Restored execution retained its originally reported exit2. This review freshly observed exit1; both are nonzero and the same exact whitespace location. A diagnostic invocation with per-command core.autocrlf=false yielded CRLF-as-whitespace noise and is not used as frozen-command evidence; no Git config was persisted."},"source_hashes":{"target_mapping":"753514d620e88d634a7398c325e003a3f20fb1c7b2e2e695bb003550c93a6569","target_source":"4dc7669e426b9fe9350ed96d81659d7d2a498a3e0ab561f22a799a12afd8767d","rollout_blockers":"a34e965c0d03abfd5b95237f7f149a1d10e85f303a825cf8d58cfd3af598a4c3"},"separate_blocker":"Unbound whole-tree format check fails in protected Task Basis outside repair candidates. Preserve as FORMAT_CHECK_SCOPE_BLOCKED, not a business finding; do not edit authorization or waive it.","authority":"Confirmed C1; architecture sections2.3,5.2-5.4.4; CONTRACTS P0-RC.1 source promotion/overlap; Data sections5,9.2 and Wire4.2.1. S3 six final claim slots not yet due, no claim of product integration.","cumulative_review":"All eight Runtime cumulative changed-file deltas/after views consumed, first-touch baseline retained. CR and report are not accepted as substitutes for source evidence; continuation report section2.5 still describes old no-reread assertions inconsistent with current code. This is supporting test/evidence assessment, not a separate expanded finding."}